Z||000000||Gokart||01-01-2000||03:42 PM||||I have a mechanic friend over right now and were trying to fix the things that the shop screwed up on but were having no luck! We found top dead center and set the timing and put in a brand new distributer w/cap and rotor. Checked plugs and wires but still runs terrible like it did on the way home from the shop Thursday. pulled plugs to find difference and there is none when we pulled no.1 wire. No change when we replaced no.1 plug and the wire reads fine on meter.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-01-2000||04:42 PM||||Do you have compression and fuel in proper quantities in number one.  Sounds mechanical if all electric checks out well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||01-01-2000||04:46 PM||||How can we check this? We don't have the equipment to check the compression. Though I know its something the service center did when changing the distributor and I picked it up after they closed Thursday. It was running ok when I brought it there with the old distributer. I even bought a new one in case this was the prob, but its not!||||reg||5
Z||000003||Phil||01-01-2000||05:03 PM||||Just have to ask- you did put the computer in diagnostic mode for timing?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phaeton||01-01-2000||05:29 PM||||To much coincidence to something complicated.  Does the injector for cyl one have positive connection.  Did a mech have the fuel rail apart and drop a piece of hangnail in just to mess with stuff?||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||01-01-2000||06:51 PM||||Make sure your plug wires are good. If you have a meter, normal(not high performance) wires are supposed to have around 10K ohms of resistance for every foot of wire.(1 foot long=10K ohms, 2 feet=20K).<BR>For timing make sure you stick a paper clip(or equivalent) in the left most(driver side) upper and lower slots of the alcl connector. The connecter is just behind the black plate covering the the cig. lighter. Tach filter is another possibility. The shop may have messed it up when they pulled the distributor. The filter is a "can" just ahead of the distributor. I don't remember how to test it, but I'm sure others know. Thats all I can think of.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||01-01-2000||07:32 PM||||NO! THANK YOU! We just used the instructions that came with the timing light and didn't connect the terminals in the computer! Another thing I noticed from looking in the haynes manual to find top dead center saying to turn the crankshaft with a wrench on the pully bolt at the front of the engine while pacing finger over no.1 spark plug hole. He just turned the key quickly till I felt a large amount of air coming out of no.1 hole. Does it matter either way or am I not even a top dead center? TIA for replys....he's coming back tomorrow. Thank God!||||reg||14
Z||000007||fiero56||01-01-2000||07:38 PM||||When you feel the #1 cylinder pressurizing that will be the compression stroke. That would be the stroke to use for tdc.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gokart||01-01-2000||07:43 PM||||Then we have top dead center? Whats the difference of doing it the way we did verses the instructions in the Haynes manual? Another thing I just remembered is that the Haynes manual tells you to add timing figures for no.1 and no.4 and divide by two. He just had clamp on no.1 plug wire the whole time. Any difference there?<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 01-01-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000009||Linx||01-01-2000||08:05 PM||||You <I>have</I> to put the computer into diagnostic mode when you check the timing, otherwise you're pretty much <I>fighting</I> the computer while your adjusting the timing; you move the distributor and the computer will compensate for it.<P>man- if there's anything Ive learned about this car, it's that having the distributor off just a smidgin', and I mean a really <I>small</I> smidgen, will affect performance in a big way.<P>As for the measure of 1 & 4 and dividing the difference; man, the difference is usually so small that I have trouble nailing it down.  I dont even try anymore.<P>Like i said before, Ive got a dollar here that says that mechanic just marked the position of your old distributor and positioned the new one to match.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||01-01-2000||08:08 PM||||Seeing that you got it to run at all means that you have the dist. close enough to the right place. All you should have to do is put the jumper in the computer terminals and set to  the dist. 10 deg BTC. Somebody please add whatever I have forgotten.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Gokart||01-01-2000||08:15 PM||||I got $100 that says so! And I'm going to give them crap about putting the old oily distributer on my clean passenger side floor mat AND messed with my deck lid! Don't know why either! Took me an hour to get it back the way it was and they were forcing it shut and the two prongs on the drivers side grill weren't even in place! They are lucky that I take alot of pride in my job or they would be getting alot of crushed packages cause I'm there UPS driver. Lastly before I fix things right tomorrow: if we did feel a large burst out of no.1 hole, do we have tdc? Cause the Haynes manual has different directions. OH, I can't wait for my factory service manual to get here cause NO ONES working on my car except me....and maybe my buddy that helped me today!||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||01-01-2000||08:15 PM||||I think Haynes doesn't recommend using the starter because you could go past tdc accidentally and not know it. <P>These are four stroke engines. When you feel air coming out a sparkplug hole, that means: both valves are closed, the piston is on it's upstroke creating pressure for the combustion.<P>When I pulled my distributor to replace the o-ring, I just used the #1 plug wire. Make sure the engine is warm, do the computer thing, and hook up the light to #1 wire. <P>I haven't taken my Fiero to a shop yet. I find it saves me more money and headache to do it myself than take it to a shop and have them do it. Plus I know the work is getting done correctly.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-01-2000).]||||reg||1
